    "result_text": "All green. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) on `POST /api/owners` are now consolidated into **one derived `identityKey`** check.\n\n**`identityKey` = `normalizedTelephone` + `'|'` + (email or empty) + `'|'` + (householdId or empty)**, and a create is rejected with 409 **only when a new owner's whole key equals an existing owner's**.\n\n### New files\n- `rest/function/owner/OwnerIdentityKey.java` \u2014 central helper computing the key for either a request (`forRequest`) or a stored owner (`forOwner`), normalizing each component to the same canonical form it's stored with (telephone\u2192E.164, email\u2192trimmed lower-case, householdId derived exactly as `AssignHouseholdId` assigns it).\n- `rest/function/owner/RequireUniqueIdentity.java` \u2014 the single pipeline step; scans existing owners and throws only on a whole-key match.\n- `rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java` + `\u2026Handler.java` \u2014 409 with body `{\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/\u2026DuplicateIdentityException.yml` \u2014 escalation wiring.\n\n### Edits\n- `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml` \u2014 replaced the `uniqueTelephone`/`uniqueEmail`/`uniqueHousehold` steps with one `uniqueIdentity` step.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema (so `OwnerDto` exposes it).\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `identityKey` via `OwnerIdentityKey.forOwner(owner)`, so every owner response returns it.\n- `AssignHouseholdId.java` \u2014 updated a javadoc link to the removed class.\n\n### Removed\nThe three superseded function classes, their exceptions, handlers, and escalation YAMLs.\n\n### Behaviour change (as specified)\nBecause the telephone is now part of the key, two members of the same household (same `householdId`) with different telephones have **different** identity keys and are both allowed \u2014 previously the household check would have rejected the second. Only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n### Verification\n`./mvnw -o test` \u2192 **BUILD SUCCESS**, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `coreRejectsIdentityCollision` acceptance test passes: two owners differing only in telephone... wait \u2014 differing only in that they *share* telephone with no email/household collide on the full key \u2192 409). I also confirmed the generated `OwnerDto` and `OwnerMapperImpl` populate `identityKey`.",
